{# The patrols module as a widget dashboard (settled design: the patrols screen,
   direction G "combined"). The dashboard itself stays CLEAN — no edit controls;
   all editing (add/remove, width, drag order) happens in the widget library,
   which is a section of the one configure page.

   The widgets themselves live in _w_<id>.html.twig and are rendered by BOTH this
   screen and the library, so a preview can never drift from the real thing.
   Which widgets, how wide and in what order comes from the shell's widget framework resolving PatrolWidgets —
   the design's layout until this person changes it. #}
{% extends '@UhifadhiPatrol/base.html.twig' %}

{# A PAGE SAYS ONLY WHAT IT IS. The shell's document composes the tab title as
   page — place — brand, so naming the area here would print it twice. #}
{% block title %}Patrols{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_title %}{{ area.name }} — Patrols{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_subtitle %}Every patrol logged in this area — where they went, how far, how much of the area they reached, and what they saw. One filter drives the map, the log and the charts together.{% endblock %}

{# THE MODULE DRAWS NO CONFIGURATION BUTTON. There is one configuration entry
   per surface — the `Configure` action in the page head — and the SHELL renders
   it from this module's declared sections. A Settings button here, a kinds link
   there and a Widget library button somewhere else is what that ruling replaced.
   → Uhifadhi\Patrol\Shell\PatrolConfigurationSections #}
{% block shell_page_actions %}
    {# THE FILE ALWAYS CARRIES THE FILTER ON SCREEN — the design's Export action,
       which has no screen of its own because there is nothing to choose. CSV
       here, because on a log page "export" means the log; the tracks bundle is
       the Export & reporting widget's second row. #}
    <a class="tgl patrol-act" href="{{ path('patrol_export', {uuid: area.uuid, _format: 'csv'}|merge(filter.toQuery)) }}">{{ ux_icon('patrol:download') }}Export</a>
    {# ONE ENTRY FLOW, SO ONE ACTION. Dropping a GPX is step 1 of logging a
       patrol now, not a screen of its own, and `patrol_import` is a permanent
       redirect into this one. The screen exists only where the host runs
       SecurityBundle (it enforces patrols.record — see UhifadhiPatrolBundle), so
       the link is rendered only when its route is. #}
    {% if recordScreens %}
        <a class="cta" href="{{ path('patrol_log', {uuid: area.uuid}) }}">{{ ux_icon('patrol:pen-line') }}Log patrol</a>
    {% endif %}
{% endblock %}

{% block patrol_page %}
<div class="patrol-wgrid">
    {% for widget in widgets %}
        {% if widget.on %}
            <div data-w="{{ widget.id }}" class="patrol-w-{{ widget.cols }}">
                <div class="patrol-winner">
                    {{ include('@UhifadhiPatrol/dashboard/_w_' ~ widget.id ~ '.html.twig') }}
                </div>
            </div>
        {% endif %}
    {% endfor %}
</div>
{% endblock %}
